From: NixOS maintainers <maintainers@nixos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: compiler: match glibc 2.42 __attribute_const__ definition

glibc 2.42 defines __attribute_const__ as __attribute__((__const__)) in
sys/cdefs.h.  The kernel tools header previously defined it as empty.
GCC 15 warns on macro redefinition to a different token sequence.

Change the kernel tools definition to match glibc so both define the
same token sequence; GCC then treats the redefinition as identical and
emits no diagnostic.  This is also semantically correct: functions
annotated with __attribute_const__ in the tools are genuinely pure.

--- a/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
+++ b/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 
 #ifndef __attribute_const__
-# define __attribute_const__
+# define __attribute_const__ __attribute__((__const__))
 #endif
 
 #ifndef __maybe_unused
